-- title:
--   Eichler–Shimura quadratic relation for Frobenius on the eigenplane
-- statement:
--   Let $M$ be a positive natural number, $g$ a weight-two cusp form on $\Gamma_0(M)$ which is a newform (a normalised eigenform whose eigensystem does not already occur at a proper divisor of $M$), $\lambda$ a prime, $S$ a finite set of natural numbers, and $O'$ a complete discrete valuation ring of characteristic zero with finite residue field in which $\lambda$ lies in the maximal ideal. Let $\chi_g$ be a ring homomorphism from the level-$M$ weight-two Hecke algebra generated away from $S\setminus\{\lambda\}$ to $\mathbb{C}$ sending each $T_\ell$ to the $\ell$-th $q$-coefficient of $g$, let $\iota$ map the image of $\chi_g$ into $O'$, assume $\lambda\in S$, every prime divisor of $M$ lies in $S$, $\lambda\nmid M$, and that $\iota\chi_g(T_\lambda)$ is a unit. Let $O''$ be a further such ring, a finite $O'$-algebra via a local homomorphism and a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-algebra, with fraction field $K$. Equip $J_0(M)$, the degree-zero divisor class group of the modular function field of level $M$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, with its Hecke-algebra action, and its $\lambda$-adic Tate module $T$ (sequences $x$ with $x_0=0$ and $\lambda\cdot x_{n+1}=x_n$) with a $\mathbb{Z}_\lambda$-structure acting levelwise through $\mathbb{Z}/\lambda^n$. Assume given: a monoid homomorphism $\rho_M$ from $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ to $O''$-endomorphisms of $O''\otimes_{\mathbb{Z}_\lambda}T$ which on pure tensors is the Galois action on $T$, and is adically continuous; a ring homomorphism $T_M$ from $\mathrm{HeckeAlg}=\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell]$ acting on pure tensors by the Hecke action; and a $K$-subspace $W$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes T)$ of dimension $2$, stable under all $\rho_M(\sigma)$ base-changed to $K$, on which the generator attached to each prime $\ell\nmid M$ with $\ell\notin S$ acts by the scalar $\iota\chi_g(T_\ell)$, on which every Frobenius element at such $\ell$ (for any valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $\ell$ non-invertible) has trace that same scalar, and on which the generator at $\lambda$ acts by $a:=\iota\chi_g(T_\lambda)$. The conclusion: for every valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ in which $\lambda$ is not a unit, every $K$-subspace $L$ of $K\otimes_{O''}(O''\otimes T)$ such that $\rho_M(\tau)w-w\in L$ for all $\tau$ in the inertia subgroup of $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ and all $w\in W$, every $\sigma$ lying in the decomposition subgroup of $A$ and acting on the residue field of $A$ by $x\mapsto x^{\lambda}$, and every $w\in W$, one has $\rho_M(\sigma)^2w-a\,\rho_M(\sigma)w+\lambda w\in L$, scalars being taken in $K$.
--
--   This is the Eichler–Shimura congruence relation in the form needed for a weight-two newform at a prime $\lambda$ of good reduction: Frobenius satisfies its expected quadratic $X^2-a_\lambda(g)X+\lambda$ on the eigenplane, up to the subspace $L$ generated by the inertial displacements. It supplies the numerical half of the local description at $\lambda$ and is used, together with the existence of a decomposition-stable line, in [`CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_galoisRepAdic_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_unitRoot_smul_mem_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.IsNewform.exists_galoisRepAdic_ordinaryLine_frobenius_sub_unitRoot_smul_mem_of_not_dvd) to identify the unit root of that quadratic as the Frobenius eigenvalue on the unramified quotient.
